    "explanation": "Both of you: the dispute is over the $4.00 cancellation-fee line on trip TRP-00204 (the separate $0.50 platform fee is not contested). The rider's claim succeeds and the $4.00 is refunded in full.\n\nThe operative clause is POL-NS-04, and all three of its limbs hold on the platform's own records. (a) EV-CHAT-00204 shows the rider sent locating/coordinating messages inside the waiting window: MSG-00204-001 (12:41:05) names her position ('im at the entrance 3 phv pickup point') and asks which car is his, and MSG-00204-003 (12:44:40) states she cannot see the vehicle. (b) The driver never answered: there is no driver message anywhere in the log, both rider messages were delivered and read (12:41:22 and 12:44:52), and EV-TRIP-00204's in_app_calls array is empty, so the 120-second reply window lapsed with neither a reply nor a call. (c) EV-GPS-00204's rider_track is present and complete: 105 of 105 fixes sit inside the 150 m rider-presence radius for LARGE_VENUE, worst case 39.93 m from the pin — not merely a majority. POL-NS-04 therefore exonerates the rider and refunds the cancellation fee in full, with no driver compensation payable.\n\nThe driver's citations are answered. The driver is right that POL-NS-01 limbs (a) to (d) are made out on the face of the record: there is a driver 'arrived' event at 12:41:50; the trace places the driver inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius (closest approach 94.94 m) across a continuous 340-second run from 12:41:50 to 12:47:30; that dwell exceeds the 300-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec); and the trip was terminated by the driver at 12:47:30 with no boarding event and the reason code RIDER_UNREACHABLE. But POL-NS-01 makes the fee stand only 'where all four conditions hold and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces them', and POL-NS-04 is one of those clauses and is fully satisfied. That same threshold defeats the driver's POL-NS-07 claim: compensation of 80% of $4.00, that is $3.20, is payable only where no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee, so the anti-farming check is never reached and no compensation is due. The driver's remaining points are accepted but change nothing: POL-NS-05 is not engaged (the marker is true — at 12:41:50 the driver was inside the radius, not more than 300 m away, and the trace's only non-zero speed, 24.9 km/h, is not tied to the marker fix), and POL-NS-06 yields no shortfall (340 s against a 300 s minimum, a surplus of 40 s, with a single in-geofence interval and nothing to accumulate). The suggestion that the rider's narrative ('Entrance 1') contradicts her message is rejected: the message named Entrance 3, which is exactly the pickup label on EV-TRIP-00204, so it is the locating message POL-NS-04(a) contemplates rather than a discrepancy.\n\nOn weight: every artifact carrying the deciding facts — EV-TRIP-00204, EV-GPS-00204 and EV-CHAT-00204 — is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, and no limb of POL-NS-08(a) to (d) is engaged, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap on this ruling is 1.0. EV-ADVIS-00204-01 is MISSING at weight_multiplier 0.0 (issue MISSING_ARTIFACT); both sides disclosed it, it carries no deciding fact and is relied on by neither, so it does not move the cap.\n\nThe monetary effect is $4.00, below the $8.00 execution threshold, so this provisional ruling executes on issue. Either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04. No referral is produced: no clause of this category directs one on these facts (POL-NS-05(ii) is not engaged and POL-NS-07's packet direction never fires because the anti-farming check does not trip)."
  },
