    "explanation": "This ruling concerns the $4.00 cancellation-fee line on trip TRP-00204 (EV-FARE-00204: cancellation_fee 4.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). The separate 0.50 platform fee is not part of the contested amount and is untouched.\n\nTo the driver: your anchor case is made out on the record. EV-TRIP-00204 carries the 'arrived' event at 12:41:50, and EV-GPS-00204 places the first qualifying in-geofence fix at that same timestamp, with the driver's closest approach to the pin at 94.94 m — inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE radius. The dwell is a single continuous 340-second in-radius run (12:41:50 to 12:47:30, 35 qualifying fixes on unbroken 10-second telemetry), against a free waiting period of 300 seconds read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec. The termination at 12:47:30 falls after the dwell elapsed and is coded RIDER_UNREACHABLE, one of the three codes POL-NS-01(d) recognises. So all four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold, POL-NS-05 is not engaged (no false marker: the 24.9 km/h reading is not tied to the arrival fix, and the marker fix is 94.94 m from the pin, not more than 300 m), and POL-NS-06 finds no shortfall (the derived shortfall is minus 40 seconds, a surplus). Your POL-NS-08/POL-NS-09 point is correct — the trace, chat log and fare line are all intact, so nothing is down-weighted and nothing escalates on integrity grounds.\n\nBut POL-NS-01 makes the fee chargeable only where all four limbs hold AND no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces them, and POL-NS-04 displaces it. All three limbs of POL-NS-04 are satisfied. (a) The rider sent locating messages during the waiting window: MSG-00204-003 at 12:44:40 ('i still cannot see u leh' — a statement she cannot see the vehicle) and MSG-00204-001 at 12:41:05, which names her own position ('entrance 3 phv pickup point') and asks which car the driver is in. (b) The driver replied to neither and placed no call — both rider messages were delivered and read (12:41:22 and 12:44:52), trip_record.in_app_calls is an empty array, and the 120-second windows after both messages expired (12:43:22 and 12:46:40) with silence. (c) The rider's own track is present and qualifying: 105 of 105 fixes inside the 150 m LARGE_VENUE rider-presence radius, mean 21.08 m and worst case 39.93 m from the pin — not merely a majority, but every fix.\n\nYour POL-NS-03 and 'entrance inconsistency' argument is rejected. The rider's chat named Entrance 3, which is exactly the registered pickup label in EV-TRIP-00204 ('Jurong Point, PHV Pickup Point, Entrance 3'); POL-NS-04 does not require the rider to name an entrance at all, and on this record there is no wrong-entrance finding to make. POL-NS-03 in any event does not apply, because your stationary fixes are inside the POL-NS-02 arrival radius, not outside it within 400 m.\n\nConsequence: the $4.00 cancellation fee is refunded in full to the rider and no driver compensation is payable — POL-NS-04 ends the matter 'with no driver compensation payable', and POL-NS-07 conditions its payout on the fee's not being displaced. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check (no_show_terminations_30d 3 against 142 completed trips) is therefore not reached; your own claim on that point is noted but immaterial. No referral fires: POL-NS-05(ii) is not triggered (no false arrival), and no other referral-producing clause is in play.\n\nConfidence: the deciding facts are carried by the trip record, the GPS trace, the chat log and the fare breakdown, each COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and no POL-NS-08(a)–(d) impairment applies. The MISSING traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00204-01, weight 0.0) carries no deciding fact and is neutral, as both sides accept. Confidence 0.90, above the 0.70 floor, so the ruling issues rather than escalating."
