    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the events; they differ on who bears the $4.00 cancellation fee, and the answer is the rider.\n\nThe driver did perform, and that finding is accepted. POL-NS-01's four limbs are made out: the trip record carries an 'arrived' event at 12:41:50 (EV-TRIP-00204); the GPS trace places the driver inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius from that same timestamp for a continuous run of 340 seconds across 35 qualifying fixes (EV-GPS-00204, derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run), against the 300-second free waiting period the trip record's own platform_policy.free_wait_sec carries; and the trip was terminated by the driver at 12:47:30 under reason code RIDER_UNREACHABLE, after that dwell had elapsed. The $4.00 fee line is the platform figure in force and reconciles with the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00204).\n\nBut POL-NS-01 makes the fee chargeable only 'where all four conditions hold and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces them', and POL-NS-04 displaces it. All three of its limbs hold. (a) The chat log carries two rider messages inside the waiting window, both locating and coordinating: MSG-00204-001 at 12:41:05 - 'hi im at the entrance 3 phv pickup point, which car ah?' - naming her own position and asking for the driver's, and MSG-00204-003 at 12:44:40 - 'boss? i still cannot see u leh'. (b) The driver never replied and never called: the log holds no driver message at all, both rider messages were delivered and read (12:41:22 and 12:44:52), and trip_record.in_app_calls is an empty array, so the 120-second reply windows (expiring 12:43:22 and 12:46:40) passed in silence before the driver cancelled at 12:47:30. (c) The rider's own track is present and complete: 105 of 105 qualifying fixes fall inside the 150 m rider-presence radius for LARGE_VENUE, mean 21.08 m and worst 39.93 m from the pin (EV-GPS-00204, derived.rider_presence), so POL-NS-11 is not engaged and the test runs and passes. POL-NS-04 therefore refunds the $4.00 cancellation-fee line in full and states that no driver compensation is payable.\n\nOn the specific arguments. The driver's point that the rider's filing says 'Entrance 1' while her own message and the pickup label say 'Entrance 3' is noted, but it decides nothing: the driver's stationary fixes sit inside the arrival radius, so this is not a POL-NS-03 wrong-entrance case, and POL-NS-04's limbs turn on the message text, the absence of any reply or call, and the rider's measured position - all objective, all favouring the rider. The driver's POL-NS-07 claim for 80 percent of the fee (SGD 3.20 of SGD 4.00, EV-FARE-00204) is rejected for the same reason POL-NS-01 is displaced: POL-NS-07 pays only where no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee. The anti-farming check would not have tripped in any event - driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 3, below the required 4, and 3/142 = 0.021, below the required 0.08 - so nothing else withholds compensation. POL-NS-05 is not engaged: at the 12:41:50 marker the driver was inside the radius and holding position, so neither the 300 m nor the 15 km/h trigger is met and there is no false-arrival referral. POL-NS-06's shortfall route is closed on the arithmetic: 340 seconds of dwell exceeds the 300-second minimum by 40 seconds. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00204-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 with issue MISSING_ARTIFACT; it was disclosed by both sides and is relied on by neither, and asserting it against a missing artifact is not done here. POL-NS-10 cannot apply, because this cancellation was made by the driver, not the rider, so its grace and its limb (f) exceptions have no subject.\n\nOn evidence quality: the three artifacts carrying the deciding facts - the chat log, the GPS trace and the trip record - are all COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0 with no issue codes; the trace has 100 percent coverage, a 10-second cadence and no gaps; the chat log holds exactly the three entries the trip record's chat_message_count records. No limb of POL-NS-08(a) to (d) is engaged, so the POL-GEN-02(2) confidence cap is 1.0 and no POL-NS-09 escalation trigger arises. The monetary effect, $4.00, is below the $8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically on issue. The $0.50 platform fee is not part of the contest and is undisturbed. The charge is refunded to the rider and no compensation is paid to the driver."
